4.0.0 2026-10
  - Participants: 1,304 in total: 748 from v3.1, with the same participant_id, and 556 new. 19 v3.1
    participants are not in this version, because of changes to their eligibility, consent or data-sharing
    status, or because none of their recordings passed the new quality review. Ages are now whole numbers
    (v3.1 wrote them with one decimal place).
  - Recordings: 43,007 (v3.1: 27,408). To improve data quality, recordings flagged by the new automated
    recording review were excluded, including 4,641 recordings that were released in v3.1.
  - Audio files are now FLAC (lossless) instead of WAV, still 16-bit PCM, 16 kHz, mono. Where resampling
    pushed a waveform past full scale, the recording is now scaled down to its original peak instead of
    being clipped.
  - Spanish-language data: 23 participants, 744 recordings with language es-419.
  - Sessions: session_id is now the session number within the participant (ses-01, ses-02, ...) instead of
    an 8-character identifier. Each participant folder adds sub-<participant_id>_sessions.tsv.
  - Audio sidecars: added language, speech_type and the stimulus fields (stimulus_text, stimulus_source,
    stimulus_asset, stimulus_asset_n_images); prompts is replaced by the stimulus fields.
  - phenotype/task/recording.tsv grows from 11 to 31 columns, adding the task name, language, instructions,
    stimulus, speech type, recording order and timing, audio sample rate and channel count, and the device,
    platform and browser used.
  - Task names: the task_name in each audio sidecar now matches the task label in the file name (for
    example cape-v-sentences-(v2)-1 -> cape-v-sentences-v2-1). The labels of 11 recordings changed:
    high-to-low -> glides-high-to-low (3), rainbowpassage -> rainbow-passage (4), and 4 recordings labelled
    maximum-phonation-time-v2-3, -4 or -5 in v3.1 that are the second maximum phonation time (v2) recording
    of their session and are now maximum-phonation-time-v2-2. recording_id is unchanged, so v3.1 recordings
    can be matched to v4.0.0 by joining the two versions' phenotype/task/recording.tsv on recording_id.
  - phenotype/enrollment/participant.tsv adds site (a pseudonymous site label) and
    some_data_collected_remotely.
  - New tables: diagnosis/ataxia, diagnosis/essential_tremor and diagnosis/huntingtons_disease.
    productive_vocabulary moved from questionnaire/ to task/.
  - Column renames: CAPE-V ratings _1 -> _severity and _2 -> _consistency (the unilateral vocal fold
    paralysis _2 ratings become diagnosis_uvfp_degree_*_consistency; its severity ratings keep their v3.1
    names); diagnois_bl_* -> diagnosis_bl_*; diagnosis_c_ac ->
    clinical_global_impression_voice_affecting_condition.
  - Free text: free-text answers new in this version were reviewed before release, and identifying details
    are replaced by [REDACTED].
  - Some answer options chosen by very few participants were combined.
  - Some fields are released only in this controlled-access dataset (48 columns in 6 tables; see README).
  - Phenotype JSON files now describe each table and give each column's description, question and choices.
  - New files: audio_quality_annotations.tsv and consensus_transcripts.parquet (an automated review of each
    recording and a consensus transcript), data_explorer.html, LICENSE and this CHANGES file. The README was
    rewritten.

3.1.0 2026-06
  - Released on Synapse (doi:10.7303/syn74341293.2).

3.0.0 2026-04
